wgpu-native is a native implementation of the WebGPU API with a C
interface (webgpu.h plus the wgpu.h extensions), built on the wgpu-core
Rust crates of the wgpu project.  It runs on Metal (macOS, iOS), Vulkan,
DirectX 12 and OpenGL ES, and accepts shaders in WGSL, SPIR-V and GLSL.
It is the backend used by wgpu-py and other language bindings.
